  "sections": [
    {
      "key": "quickFacts",
      "source": "planetcatfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.planetcatfish.com/common/species.php?species_id=1409",
      "html": "<ul><li>Scientific name: Kyataphisa nenga (Hamilton, 1822)</li><li>Common name: Spotfin Sea Catfish</li><li>Type locality: Estuaries of Bengal, India.</li><li>IUCN Red List category: Not Evaluated</li></ul>"
    },
    {
      "key": "distribution",
      "source": "planetcatfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.planetcatfish.com/common/species.php?species_id=1409",
      "html": "<p>Indo-west Pacific: Eastern Arabian Sea, Bay of Bengal and western central Pacific.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "reproduction",
      "source": "planetcatfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.planetcatfish.com/common/species.php?species_id=1409",
      "html": "<p>Unreported in the aquarium.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "notes",
      "source": "planetcatfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.planetcatfish.com/common/species.php?species_id=1409",
      "html": "<p>Unfortunately, the only way you can reliably tell N. nenga from Arius maculatus is in the teeth. However, N. nenga frequently has a dorsal spine that is as long as the head (the dorsal spine in A. maculatus is always shorter than the head).</p>"
    },
